   <p><note place="header">56</note>
<lb/><date when="1864-02-14">Feby 14<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">th</hi></hi> <gap/>5</date>
<lb/>Dr <persName ref="cwgk:N00004347">R. C. Hewitt</persName>
<lb/>Chr<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">m</hi></hi> <orgName ref="cwgk:O00012970">Med<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">l</hi></hi> Board</orgName>.
<lb/><placeName ref="cwgk:P00000337">Louisville</placeName> <placeName ref="cwgk:P001800">Ky</placeName>.
<lb/>Sir</p>
<p>I have the honor to request that your Board will examine Dr<persName ref="cwgk:N00013513"> B. F Slaughter</persName> touching his qualifications for the position of Asst Surg, he having produced satisfactory evidence to this Dep<hi rend="sup">t</hi> of his loyalty and good standing.</p>
<p>By command of the<persName ref="cwgk:N001000"> Governor</persName>.
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00000873">D, W, Lindsey</persName>
<lb/>Insp<hi rend="sup">t</hi> &amp; Adj Gen<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">l</hi></hi><orgName ref="cwgk:O001025"> Ky</orgName></p>
  </body>
